# Printable reports

Word and PDF are one filled `.docx`. Do not paint a report page in HTML, canvas, or a hand-built `.doc` string.

## Template

- Super admin uploads the `.docx`. School staff only download.
- The file must contain `{{schoolName}}` and `{{schoolLogo}}` (header or top of the page). Reject an upload that lacks either tag.
- One repeating data row uses `{{#rows}}` … `{{/rows}}` and the report’s column tags.
- Excel is the rows only. It does not use the Word file.

## Download

- Fill `{{schoolName}}` from the school record for the report language: Arabic name when the report is Arabic, English name when English. If one language is empty, use the other.
- Embed `{{schoolLogo}}` from the school logo in settings. A missing logo leaves the name and an empty logo spot.
- PDF is that filled file converted (`soffice`). Do not draw a second layout for PDF.

```ts
// BAD — HTML letterhead painted into Word/PDF
applyWordPageOrientation(layoutHtml)

// GOOD — one Word template, filled from the school
renderReportDocx(template, { schoolName, rows }, logoBytes)
```

The first report on this path is due and late payments (`report-docx.ts`). New printable reports follow it. Reports that already paint HTML stay on that path until they are moved.
